# The skip between acts (scripts/acts.gd; Alex, 2026-11-24: "the time skip is the player's choice").
# Each act's last goal sets act_ready; her bed's "Begin the next chapter…" or the Esc menu's row then
# plays act<N>_begin, never on its own. The first choice is the confirm: "Not yet" changes nothing.
# @act next makes the skip (the act, her age and model, the calendar, act_ready cleared, the next
# act's goals; going into Act 2, Gran's passing and the end of her rent), @act card shows the
# montage card of what she has. With a partner (scripts/partners.gd), going into Act 2 he proposes on
# the porch, and going into Act 3 they marry in the town square ("@if partner <id>"); without one,
# neither scene plays. The format is at the top of scripts/story.gd.
# Every line here is a DRAFT for Alex.

== act2_begin
@requires act_ready
? Begin the next chapter? Twenty-five years will pass, and everything you own comes with you.
- Begin it. -> go
- Not yet.
@end
@label go
@fade out 1.5
@act next
@title Twenty-five years later
@act card
@fade in 1.5
Nora (warm): Fifty. Somewhere along the way the farm stopped being Gran's and started being mine.
> The needles are the same pair. Her hands know them better now.
@if partner rowan -> rowan
@if partner lars -> lars
@if partner gary -> gary
@end
# --- the proposal, on the porch at dusk
@label rowan
@fade out 1.0
@time 18.5
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@place rowan 11.1 3.0 270
@face nora rowan
@face rowan nora
@camera between rowan nora 5.5
@fade in 1.2
> The porch light Gran never fixed is still broken. Rowan fixed everything else.
Rowan (neutral): Twenty-five years of walking your fence. Thought I'd ask before the next twenty-five.
> He opens his hand. A plain silver ring, threaded on a loop of her own grey wool.
Rowan (warm): Marry me. If you want. No rush. Well. Some rush. I'm not getting younger. You are, somehow.
? Rowan is asking you to marry him.
- "Yes. Of course, yes." -> rowan_yes | romance rowan +5
- "Yes. What took you so long?" -> rowan_tease | romance rowan +5
@label rowan_yes
Rowan (happy): ...Good. That's good. I'd practised a longer one.
@goto proposed
@label rowan_tease
Rowan (wry): Sheep don't rush. Neither do I. You knew that.
@goto proposed
@label lars
@fade out 1.0
@time 5.8
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@place lars 11.1 3.0 270
@face nora lars
@face lars nora
@camera between lars nora 5.5
@fade in 1.2
> First light on the porch. Lars has brought the radio over from the barn, and it's playing a slow one.
Lars (warm): So. I've been meaning to ask. For about twenty-five years. No rush, I said. Turns out I meant it.
> He goes down on one knee, which takes him a moment, and holds up a ring on a twist of baling twine.
Lars (happy): Marry me? All good if you need to think. Please don't think too long.
? Lars is asking you to marry him.
- "Yes. Yes, you lovely man." -> lars_yes | romance lars +5
- "Get up before your knee goes. Yes." -> lars_tease | romance lars +5
@label lars_yes
Lars (happy): Yes! She said yes! The sheep heard that. Everybody heard that.
@goto proposed
@label lars_tease
Lars (wry): Bit late for the knee. Worth it, though.
@goto proposed
@label gary
@fade out 1.0
@time 19.0
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@place gary 11.1 3.0 270
@face nora gary
@face gary nora
@camera between gary nora 5.5
@fade in 1.2
> Gary on her porch, in a new blazer, holding a small velvet box like it might go off.
Gary (neutral): I've sold four hundred houses. I've never been this nervous about a closing.
Gary (warm): You never wanted to move up. You were already where you wanted to be. I'd like to be there too.
> The box opens. The ring is very shiny. Of course it is.
Gary (wry): Marry me. Please note the please. I don't say it to clients.
? Gary is asking you to marry him.
- "Yes. No conditions." -> gary_yes | romance gary +5
- "Yes. But the blazer stays at the wedding." -> gary_tease | romance gary +5
@label gary_yes
Gary (happy): Sold. Best deal I ever made, and I didn't even have to pitch it.
@goto proposed
@label gary_tease
Gary (wry): The blazer is the wedding. But fine. Yes. Yes!
@label proposed
@set proposed
@journal note The proposal | Twenty-five years on, and he asked me on Gran's porch. I said yes.
@fade out 1.0
@home rowan off
@home lars off
@home gary off
@camera player
@fade in 1.0

== act3_begin
@requires act_ready
? Begin the next chapter? Twenty-five years will pass, and everything you own comes with you.
- Begin it. -> go
- Not yet.
@end
@label go
@fade out 1.5
@act next
@title Twenty-five years later
@act card
@fade in 1.5
Nora (warm): Seventy-five. The whole valley wears my sweaters now. Imagine that.
@if partner rowan -> rowan
@if partner lars -> lars
@if partner gary -> gary
@end
# --- the wedding, in the town square: Wren marries them by the fountain
@label rowan
@fade out 1.0
@time 15.0
@weather clear
@place nora 52.5 2.4 90
@place rowan 53.6 2.4 270
@place wren 53.05 3.6 180
@place rosa 51.2 4.6 30
@place giorgio 54.9 4.6 330
@place lars 50.6 3.4 60
@face nora rowan
@face rowan nora
@camera between rowan nora 5.5
@fade in 1.4
> The whole town has come to the square. Rosa is already crying. Giorgio has baked a cake taller than he is.
Wren (warm): Rowan. Nora. Took you long enough. Shall we?
Rowan (neutral): I'm not good with words.
Rowan (warm): So. You. Always. That's it. That's the speech.
Nora (warm): That's a good speech.
Wren (happy): Then by the power vested in me by Maple Grove, and a stack of forms I filled in myself: you're married.
@goto wed
@label lars
@fade out 1.0
@time 15.0
@weather clear
@place nora 52.5 2.4 90
@place lars 53.6 2.4 270
@place wren 53.05 3.6 180
@place rosa 51.2 4.6 30
@place giorgio 54.9 4.6 330
@place rowan 50.6 3.4 60
@face nora lars
@face lars nora
@camera between lars nora 5.5
@fade in 1.4
> The whole town has come to the square. Rosa is already crying. Someone has brought the barn's radio, and it's playing a slow one.
Wren (warm): Lars. Nora. Ready?
Lars (happy): Been ready for fifty years. No rush, though.
Lars (warm): I don't need anywhere else. I never did. Now I'm sure.
Nora (warm): Me too.
Wren (happy): Then by the power vested in me by Maple Grove, and a stack of forms I filled in myself: you're married.
@goto wed
@label gary
@fade out 1.0
@time 15.0
@weather clear
@place nora 52.5 2.4 90
@place gary 53.6 2.4 270
@place wren 53.05 3.6 180
@place rosa 51.2 4.6 30
@place giorgio 54.9 4.6 330
@place lars 50.6 3.4 60
@face nora gary
@face gary nora
@camera between gary nora 5.5
@fade in 1.4
> The whole town has come to the square. Rosa is already crying. Gary's blazer is, for once, not the smartest thing in sight.
Wren (warm): Gary. Nora. Ready?
Gary (warm): I've had my vows written for a month. I've thrown them all away. Here's the short one.
Gary (neutral): I got my gate. It's yours. It's always been yours.
Nora (warm): That's the best pitch you've ever made.
Wren (happy): Then by the power vested in me by Maple Grove, and a stack of forms I filled in myself: you're married.
@label wed
> The square goes up in a cheer. Rosa blows her nose like a trumpet.
@set married
@journal note The wedding | Married in the square by the fountain, with the whole town watching. Rosa cried the entire time.
@fade out 1.2
@home rowan off
@home lars off
@home gary off
@home wren off
@home rosa off
@home giorgio off
@camera player
@fade in 1.0

== act4_begin
@requires act_ready
? Begin the last chapter? Twenty-five years will pass, and everything you own comes with you.
- Begin it. -> go
- Not yet.
@end
@label go
@fade out 1.5
@act next
@title Twenty-five years later
@act card
@fade in 1.5
Nora (warm): A hundred years old, and still knitting. Gran would laugh.
